    summary: "Here\'s a summary of UI (User Interface) web GitHub repositories for the specified agent frameworks:\n\n**AutoGen Studio**\nAutoGen Studio is a low-code interface built on Microsoft\'s AutoGen framework for rapidly prototyping, managing, and interacting with AI agents and multi-agent workflows[1][2][3][4]. It features a user-friendly drag-and-drop interface for defining agents and workflows, interactive chat sessions, and skill integration[1]. The code for AutoGen Studio is available on GitHub under the `microsoft/autogen` repository[5][3]. It\'s important to note that AutoGen is now in maintenance mode, and new users are encouraged to explore Microsoft Agent Framework[5].\n\n**Agency Swarm**\nAgency Swarm is a framework for building multi-agent applications that extends the OpenAI Agents SDK[6]. The primary GitHub repository is `VRSEN/agency-swarm`[6][7]. It offers a Web UI through `agency.copilot_demo()` and a terminal UI (TUI) that automatically sets up on the first run[6]. Related GitHub repositories include:\n*   `VRSEN/agency-swarm-api-railway-template`: Demonstrates deploying an Agency Swarm agency as a FastAPI application with a Gradio UI[8].\n*   `VRSEN/agentswarm-cli`: A terminal application for running and testing Agency Swarm projects[9].\n\n**CrewAI UI**\nSeveral GitHub repositories offer UI solutions for CrewAI, a framework for orchestrating role-playing autonomous AI agents[10][11]:\n*   `amazingnerd/CrewAI-UI`: Provides a simplified, intuitive user interface for creating and managing AI crews without requiring coding[10].\n*   `zinyando/crewai_chat_ui`: A package that enables users to chat with their CrewAI crews through a modern web-based UI, managing chat history and supporting multiple conversation threads[12].\n*   `LangGraph-GUI/CrewAI-GUI-Qt`: Features a node-based interface for designing complex AI agent interactions via drag-and-drop, with JSON export capabilities[13].\n*   `strnad/CrewAI-Studio`: Offers a user-friendly, multi-platform GUI for managing and running CrewAI agents and tasks, supporting Conda and virtual environments without requiring coding[14].\n\n**openai/swarm**\nThe `openai/swarm` GitHub repository describes an \"Educational framework exploring ergonomic, lightweight multi-agent orchestration\"[15]. However, OpenAI states that Swarm has been replaced by the OpenAI Agents SDK, which is its production-ready successor[15]. Despite this, there are community efforts to build UIs for Swarm:\n*   YouTube tutorials and associated GitHub repositories demonstrate how to build web UIs for OpenAI\'s Swarm applications using libraries like Panel and Streamlit[16][17][18]. For example, a demo source code for a Panel-based chat interface is available[16].\n*   `Chigala/swarmjs`: A Node.js implementation of OpenAI\'s experimental Swarm framework, with plans to develop UI components[19].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEfVWhmYYk6ARoKwOLmOfd2uvtFvlYLKReTSBzz_AwNlNw7oZftAsA5XlVHmQplzSsdADveLGmqTDdxjuLsP67ByqW_k_qzPXEHnIb2ZAk8kkte0ZDmeQI_bPMPSrEKvFoRLXs7)\n[2] [github.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEwoa6EDt2eFPvsBvTCKiw1an4N9SEUD1l4uwJWwGwOMAqgPdth5xPDXuDjNzfbVhm2q3GxYVhWnq5bB9pwrMf3qFE2h9qbaKyb2I4ZTllB7-TfiKR-gDCZ9WBpCCky9oRz-ROXqmtIIjIiqTHEVJ6TZFIDRinqEK-vRyTy-Lo8CTk49z4_Upn0Tv-31qw-rMM=)\n[3] [github.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGZa9mj5tsGxg73gJ3ABA55uLh4Gun_bww878CdJ08nMF3RT97-jx3-d17PdImf_gv9cXZR9tGZq8gYOd_sDhmBl7MLEPDE01KdofcY0eDOC03QpUTVeXj5MzCIuFpy5KWr2-HIb_-y2dd7KxsYc50cqrPNg7154RfTfGGF33QSjYAPTjA3KQ==)\n[4] [microsoft.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHl4kNm2CV8SAkg8KE3iOQ_m1E9zZg_HQbsJarvtD775a32TQdpAD-AL4ZwGsvkRB-qPDBKlQm6v_Y5fT1b3p6ltCa3e4mgZbyqzeRAa8Rezk0ZPf3xnQ8wLnIEJHlJEU0i2TQRVp5olV_ZYI1HPmCZe55TkRtD5TUVa7jGPdnOiLOITDy5YMhc7_aRaTyIHHQcu2SSCb8upCXxOy48bRsljNvyt_nL2eLQ9YRw3-eLpV-g-S30vXR