    thinking: "**Defining the App Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a good handle on the user\'s initial prompt and the desired app functionality. I\'m focusing now on defining the scope: creating a dedicated \"Open Source Agent Swarm UI Research & Architecture Workbench.\" This means interactive and comprehensive. I\'m excited by this.\n\n\n**Listing Key Features**\n\nNow, I\'m diving deep into the necessary features. I\'m compiling a comprehensive catalog and directory of open-source UIs and frameworks. Currently, I\'m working through a list, including Agency Swarm, AutoGen Studio, AgentSwarms, Langflow, Dify.ai, and the CrewAI UI ecosystem, to determine their core functionalities and how they fit into a comprehensive research hub.\n\n\n**Expanding the Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI options beyond the initial list. I\'m excited by the possibilities of **OpenHands Agent Canvas**, **PicoAgents Web UI**, **VoltAgent / SwarmJS / Open-Swarm UIs**, **Chainlit & Mesop**, and **Flowise**. Each offers unique multi-agent debugging, coordination, and visualization capabilities. Now, I am formulating a comparison matrix, enabling multi-dimensional comparison across architectures, UI paradigms, and tech stacks, for comprehensive evaluation.\n\n\n"
