  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing App Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the application\'s components now. Starting with `Header.tsx`, I\'m envisioning the logo, title (\"Agent Swarm UI Research Explorer\"), and a GitHub star count tracker. I\'m also planning quick filter switches and tab navigation within the header. This section will provide the basic layout of the application for now.\n\n\n**Exploring New Features**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the directory and in-depth profiles. I\'m especially interested in the interactive \"Swarm Topology Simulator\". Then, I\'m focusing on \"AI Research Advisor,\" which uses Gemini 3.7 Flash and web citations. The \"Stack Recommender & Boilerplate Generator\" sounds useful, too. I will add a status badge showing server and Gemini status.\n\n\n**Developing Comparison Tool**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a detailed comparison system. I\'m planning scorecard preview bars and quick action buttons for each framework. A deep profile modal will provide in-depth architecture breakdowns, quickstart guides, and feature comparisons. I\'m aiming for easy copyable code with syntax highlighting and direct links to documentation.\nFurthermore, I\'m working on a comparison matrix, enabling side-by-side analysis of up to four frameworks. It will have a comprehensive table covering core paradigms, tech stacks, and feature matrices. I will also incorporate visual scorecards, deployment difficulty assessments, and export options.\n\n\n**Visualizing Swarm Architectures**\n\nI\'m currently outlining core swarm structures: hierarchical supervision, peer handoffs, sequential pipelines, and consensus-driven debates. I\'m focusing on interactive controls, particularly simulation runs, step-by-step advancements, resets, and speed adjustments. I envision visual nodes with pulsing glows, animated message packets, and real-time token counters. A live event log will stream handoffs, executions, and human interactions, and the agent inspector is also in progress.\n\n\n**Expanding Advisor & Recommender**\n\nI\'m now integrating the node click functionality to display system prompts, tools, and metrics. Regarding the AI Research Advisor, I\'m focusing on its functionality, including preset queries and free-form input, the ability to generate reports with web grounding sources, and conversational memory. I\'m also developing the Stack Recommender, starting with an interactive 4-step questionnaire.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 802214976
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
