  }
  planner_response {
    response: "I have conducted comprehensive research on free and open-source User Interfaces (UIs) and visual platforms for AI Agent Swarms and Multi-Agent Systems, and implemented the **Agent Swarm UI Research Explorer & Architecture Workbench**.\n\nHere is a summary of the top open-source UIs and visual frameworks for agent swarms:\n\n---\n\n### Key Open-Source Swarm UIs & Frameworks\n\n| Platform / UI | Primary Focus & UI Paradigm | Stack & License | Key Strengths |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Agency Swarm** (`VRSEN/agency-swarm`) | **Web Copilot & TUI**: Dynamic peer-to-peer handoffs built on OpenAI Agents SDK. | Python (MIT) | Instant `agency.copilot_demo()` Web UI, ergonomic communication charts, zero-boilerplate handoff functions. |\n| **AutoGen Studio** (`microsoft/autogen`) | **Visual Workflow & Chat**: Declarative builder for multi-agent teams and GroupChat managers. | Python / React (MIT) | Visual skill creation, interactive session logs, preconfigured multi-agent templates, local model support. |\n| **Langflow** (`langflow-ai/langflow`) | **Node Graph Canvas**: Drag-and-drop graph canvas for multi-agent DAGs and LangGraph supervisors. | Python / React (MIT) | Visual flow builder, real-time token and step tracing, dynamic tool routing, one-click API export. |\n| **Dify.ai** (`langgenius/dify`) | **Enterprise Workflow Platform**: Multi-agent orchestration, ReAct teams, and RAG knowledge base. | Python / Next.js (Open Source) | Production-ready multi-tenant workspaces, parallel execution branches, extensive tool marketplace. |\n| **OpenHands** (`All-Hands-AI/OpenHands`) | **Workspace & Agent Sandbox**: Autonomous coding agent swarm with terminal and file diff viewers. | Python / React (MIT) | Isolated Docker container execution, step-by-step reasoning tree, live diff reviewer. |\n| **CrewAI UI Ecosystem** (`CrewAI-UI`, `CrewAI-Studio`) | **Control Plane & Dashboard**: Role-playing autonomous crews and sequential/hierarchical pipelines. | Python / Streamlit (MIT) | Intuitive Agent, Task, and Crew abstractions; memory modules and manager delegation. |\n| **AgentSwarms** (`AgentSwarms-fyi/agentswarms`) | **Visual Swarm Canvas**: Drag-and-drop canvas for concurrent swarms and worker pools. | TypeScript / Python (MIT) | Real-time message packet passing animation, trace inspector, parallel swarm routing. |\n| **Chainlit** (`Chainlit/chainlit`) | **Conversational Copilot**: Python web framework with nested multi-agent call trees and step debugging. | Python / React (Apache-2.0) | Rapid setup, step nesting visualizer, human-in-the-loop approval buttons. |\n| **VoltAgent** (`VoltAgent/voltagent`) | **TypeScript Platform**: Modern TypeScript agent engineering platform with supervisor coordination. | TypeScript / Node.js (Apache-2.0) | 100% native TypeScript/Next.js support, type-safe supervisor delegates. |\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built in the Application\n\n- **Research Catalog & Deep Dives**: Detailed profiles with GitHub star metrics, tech stacks, pros/cons, architecture breakdowns, and copy-pasteable installation scripts (Pip, Docker, Git).\n- **Side-by-Side Comparison Matrix**: Compare up to 4 frameworks simultaneously across multi-agent topologies (Supervisor, Peer Handoff, Sequential, Graph DAG), features, and local Ollama compatibility, with export to Markdown.\n- **Interactive Swarm Topology Simulator**: Visual node canvas with animated token packets, agent thought bubbles, and live event trace rails across 4 key topologies.\n- **AI Multi-Agent Research Advisor**: Full-stack integration with server-side Gemini 3.7 Flash and Google Search grounding to answer custom architectural questions and benchmark queries.\n- **Interactive Stack Matcher & Boilerplate Generator**: 4-step wizard that recommends frameworks based on your preferred language, UI paradigm, hosting strategy, and swarm goal."
    thinking: "**Verifying All Requirements**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` processes were successful. Now, I\'m meticulously cross-referencing all aspects of the user\'s initial request. I\'m focusing specifically on the details provided: \"do reserch for free open srce ui for agents swam\" to ensure comprehensive fulfillment. The goal is an interactive and exhaustive response.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Architecture**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to analyzing and architecting a high-value Agent Swarm UI. My research catalog is now taking shape, detailing the top open-source Swarm UIs and multi-agent platforms. I\'m actively assessing features from projects like `VRSEN/agency-swarm`, `microsoft/autogen`, and others, to understand their UI strengths and architectural choices, ensuring it is comprehensive.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have conducted comprehensive research on free and open-source User Interfaces (UIs) and visual platforms for AI Agent Swarms and Multi-Agent Systems, and implemented the **Agent Swarm UI Research Explorer & Architecture Workbench**.\n\nHere is a summary of the top open-source UIs and visual frameworks for agent swarms:\n\n---\n\n### Key Open-Source Swarm UIs & Frameworks\n\n| Platform / UI | Primary Focus & UI Paradigm | Stack & License | Key Strengths |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Agency Swarm** (`VRSEN/agency-swarm`) | **Web Copilot & TUI**: Dynamic peer-to-peer handoffs built on OpenAI Agents SDK. | Python (MIT) | Instant `agency.copilot_demo()` Web UI, ergonomic communication charts, zero-boilerplate handoff functions. |\n| **AutoGen Studio** (`microsoft/autogen`) | **Visual Workflow & Chat**: Declarative builder for multi-agent teams and GroupChat managers. | Python / React (MIT) | Visual skill creation, interactive session logs, preconfigured multi-agent templates, local model support. |\n| **Langflow** (`langflow-ai/langflow`) | **Node Graph Canvas**: Drag-and-drop graph canvas for multi-agent DAGs and LangGraph supervisors. | Python / React (MIT) | Visual flow builder, real-time token and step tracing, dynamic tool routing, one-click API export. |\n| **Dify.ai** (`langgenius/dify`) | **Enterprise Workflow Platform**: Multi-agent orchestration, ReAct teams, and RAG knowledge base. | Python / Next.js (Open Source) | Production-ready multi-tenant workspaces, parallel execution branches, extensive tool marketplace. |\n| **OpenHands** (`All-Hands-AI/OpenHands`) | **Workspace & Agent Sandbox**: Autonomous coding agent swarm with terminal and file diff viewers. | Python / React (MIT) | Isolated Docker container execution, step-by-step reasoning tree, live diff reviewer. |\n| **CrewAI UI Ecosystem** (`CrewAI-UI`, `CrewAI-Studio`) | **Control Plane & Dashboard**: Role-playing autonomous crews and sequential/hierarchical pipelines. | Python / Streamlit (MIT) | Intuitive Agent, Task, and Crew abstractions; memory modules and manager delegation. |\n| **AgentSwarms** (`AgentSwarms-fyi/agentswarms`) | **Visual Swarm Canvas**: Drag-and-drop canvas for concurrent swarms and worker pools. | TypeScript / Python (MIT) | Real-time message packet passing animation, trace inspector, parallel swarm routing. |\n| **Chainlit** (`Chainlit/chainlit`) | **Conversational Copilot**: Python web framework with nested multi-agent call trees and step debugging. | Python / React (Apache-2.0) | Rapid setup, step nesting visualizer, human-in-the-loop approval buttons. |\n| **VoltAgent** (`VoltAgent/voltagent`) | **TypeScript Platform**: Modern TypeScript agent engineering platform with supervisor coordination. | TypeScript / Node.js (Apache-2.0) | 100% native TypeScript/Next.js support, type-safe supervisor delegates. |\n\n---\n\n### What Was Built in the Application\n\n- **Research Catalog & Deep Dives**: Detailed profiles with GitHub star metrics, tech stacks, pros/cons, architecture breakdowns, and copy-pasteable installation scripts (Pip, Docker, Git).\n- **Side-by-Side Comparison Matrix**: Compare up to 4 frameworks simultaneously across multi-agent topologies (Supervisor, Peer Handoff, Sequential, Graph DAG), features, and local Ollama compatibility, with export to Markdown.\n- **Interactive Swarm Topology Simulator**: Visual node canvas with animated token packets, agent thought bubbles, and live event trace rails across 4 key topologies.\n- **AI Multi-Agent Research Advisor**: Full-stack integration with server-side Gemini 3.7 Flash and Google Search grounding to answer custom architectural questions and benchmark queries.\n- **Interactive Stack Matcher & Boilerplate Generator**: 4-step wizard that recommends frameworks based on your preferred language, UI paradigm, hosting strategy, and swarm goal."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 670920662
