  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Concept**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the \"Littlebird\" UI screenshot. My focus is on understanding the design principles, especially how it achieves that clean, modern workspace aesthetic. I\'m looking at specific elements to identify key connectors and the user interface patterns that make it visually appealing. I want to determine the design techniques at play.\n\n\n**Developing Functional Concepts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a functional concept based on the \"Littlebird\" design. I envision a multi-tab window bar akin to the original screenshot, but incorporating real connectors and integrations. There will be a clean sidebar with beige/cream/neutral tones, a projects tree, and a prompt box with a \"+\" icon. A model selector (\"Max\"), a microphone, and a send arrow will also be present.\n\nI\'ve outlined specific elements such as a window top bar with toggle, navigation arrows, browser/desktop-style tabs (with icons like chat bubbles), a new tab \"+\" button, and standard window controls. The left sidebar will include the logo and navigation items. I\'m focusing on features and layout details.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation & Content**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the sidebar navigation, adding \"New Chat\", \"Search\", \"Meeting Notes\", and \"Routines\" as active pills with the described color palette. I\'m also including a \"Projects\" section with an expandable \"ai\" folder. In the main content area, I\'ve added a greeting, a subtitle with the real-time date, and a centered prompt box with the specified action buttons. I\'ve included the \"Update ready\" card and user profile details at the bottom of the sidebar.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 102725550
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
