  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Edits**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the required edits for user profiles. Specifically, I\'m examining how to dynamically display the user\'s first name (\"Vijay\" from \"vijay.goona@gmail.com\") within the app\'s UI, starting with updates in `App.tsx`. I\'m going through the `user` state and determining if and how to update it.\n\n\n**Refining Profile Display**\n\nI\'ve been refining how user information, particularly the name, is displayed across the application. I\'m focusing on the avatar initials in `Sidebar.tsx`, using the name \"VG\". I also updated the greeting header to show the user\'s first name, which will now say \"What\'s the next step, Vijay?\". I\'m also ensuring that these new settings are reflected in `data/connectors.ts` and `server.ts`.\n\n\n**Designing Sidebar Interaction**\n\nI\'m now designing the interactive hover-reveal for the sidebar\'s functionality. My plan involves a smooth glide-in effect on hover or when `isHoveringSidebar` is true, and a smooth glide-out on mouse leave. I\'m exploring an auto-peek/pin toggle for user control, with auto-peek as the default. To accomplish this, I\'m going to set up a proximity strip along the left edge of the screen, acting as a peek trigger.\n\n\n**Implementing Connector Interactivity**\n\nI\'ve just added complete interactivity to all connector icons in `MainChatView.tsx`, enabling hover cards, tooltips, and direct attachment to prompts. I\'ve also made tool badges clickable for status and item viewing. In `ConnectorDrawer.tsx`, I\'ve implemented \"Ask AI about this item,\" \"Insert Item,\" and \"Add Item\" buttons for user interaction. I\'ve also integrated a live search with a sync animation. Finally, I\'ve implemented a \"Ground in Next Query\" button.\n\n**Clearing Initial Chat Data**\n\nNow I\'m cleaning up the initial chat experience. I removed those two fake pre-populated chat history tabs, so now the initial state is a clean \"New Chat\" tab with that clean greeting \"What\'s the next step, Vijay?\".\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 869798213
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
