  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Hover Interaction**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing a hover-based interaction for the sidebar. The goal is a proximity-based reveal, hiding the sidebar when the mouse moves away. I\'m exploring how best to handle this in `App.tsx` and considering the smoothest way to trigger the reveal and hide states.\n\n\n**Implementing Hover Mechanics**\n\nI\'ve established the sidebar\'s state using `isSidebarHovered` and `isSidebarPinned`, with the latter defaulting to `false` for hover behavior. I\'m implementing a proximity trigger strip, which will change the `isSidebarHovered` to `true` when the mouse enters the rail or sidebar area. The sidebar will transition smoothly using Tailwind, and leave smoothly using the same technique when the mouse leaves. Finally, I\'m integrating a pin button for permanent display, but keeping the default hover behavior.\n\n\n**Displaying User Profile**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the user profile display. I\'m extracting \"Gaman\" from the email or profile for display as the first word and initial avatar, and I\'m updating `MainChatView.tsx` with `\"What\'s the next step, Gaman?\"`. Furthermore, I\'ve initialized the tabs in `App.tsx` with a clean starting chat. I\'ve stripped the `tabs` initialization from fake chats, ensuring only a new chat option.\n\n\n"
